A||||4||Cheever3000||Let's all come together.  (long speech)||||2||
Z||000000||Cheever3000||10-25-2001||12:29 AM||||I started to add the following to the CFOG-I "Announcement" thread in the club section, but knew it wouldn't get much visibility.  Cliff, forgive me if putting it in O/T was wrong, but I thought it to be less of an inconvenience here than in the General section.<BR>= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =<P>I just want to say that I can understand skepticism of CFOG-I based on (1)-past large-club experiences, and (2)-questioning what will be accomplished.  <P>To the first: there is really no reason for this effort <I>not</I> to succeed!  Even if the ball is dropped by its current leadership, new leadership will be elected.  Meanwhile, any concerns, objections or disagreements will be given utmost attention, with an attitude of cooperation.  In our discussions during the initial planning of this, we pledged to be <B>responsible</B> and <B>accountable</B> to all Fiero owners.  We only want what you want, because we <I>are</I> you.  Our intentions are to unite and to represent.  Not to sell parts, T-shirts or anything else.<P>Secondly, regarding what is to be accomplished, and what <I>can</I> be done:  the answer to that is <I>whatever you want</I>.  Okay, we realize you want to see some tangible evidence... fair enough.  The first magazine will be out I believe by the end of November (Terry or Lisa: correct me if I'm wrong), and that's the first step.  There's a whole lot we want to do once we get out of first gear.  But you can't steer a bus that's not moving, no matter how many or how few people are on it.  You probably have ideas we haven't thought of, and if so, bring em on, but more importantly, come aboard and help us fulfill those aspirations.<P>Because we're an open book, I'll be honest and tell you we've gotten some feedback that says things like "it's been tried and failed", and "what will we get in return for our dues", and "I'll wait and see what happens".  Fair enough, those are <I>reasonable and valid</I> concerns.  Nobody's going to ridicule anybody for skepticism.  I'm just saying not only <B>can</B> this work, but it most definitely <B>will</B> work if we unite.  Look at the success of Cliff's Forum, and look at how the Fiero List continues even without moderation.  Those are excellent communication tools, and they work well.  We're not even trying to dismantle FOCOA - Phil Huff has done much for the Fiero community - heck, we even have a link to it on our website.  But let's tie the whole package together - as it <B>should</B> be for fans of a wonderful car that was only made for 5 years - with an organization that has the potential to do anything we can dream of doing.  Look what other car enthusiasts have.  We have <B>more</B> reason than most of them for having a dynamic successful organization which not only unites our own people, but which has a public relations effort - speaking with one voice to proclaim the kind of people Fiero owners are, and to dispel the mysteries and myths about our cars.<P>Take another look at the website (www.cfog-i.org).  It's already changed from when we made the first announcement.  Look at the clubs that have signed on.  Read the guestbook.  Come back to it in a few weeks.  We're continually evolving and growing.  Your input can give better direction to that growth.<P>I'm not just enjoying sitting here typing all this... I really feel it and believe in it.  I have invested myself in it.  My heart belongs to all you guys out there: the collectors, the racers, the customizers, the car show people, and the low-budget owner who's lucky to keep it running.  And I'm saying let's do it, and let's do it right.  We need this.  Don't let past disappointments prevent what needs to be done.  Maybe even more importantly, let's do it for the future generations.  All the club websites talk about the "preservation" of these fine cars - well, if we can't get some kind of Super Glue to keep us all together, then what's left of the Fieros will be gone in the not-too-distant future.  Think about it.  <P>For those who are content to sit around and wait, I respect you.  But there really is no reason to hold back.  What if everybody does it?  That may only <B>ensure</B> failure.  Tell you what -- for the first person to contact me and ask for it, I will pay their first years' dues out of my own pocket.  I want you to come with us and help guide the future of Fiero preservation.<P>Whatever happens, I love you guys.  It's really the <I>people</I> that make this hobby so great, not the plastic & steel which is sitting in my driveway awaiting replacement parts.  I'll be here for you any way I can, whether you sign up for CFOG-I or not.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I><BR>Vice President, <A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||2
Z||000001||Return of Fiero||10-25-2001||12:18 PM||||im not lookin' for anything special, nor will i accept, if offered, my question is if you can contact me about you letter, in private.<BR>myke<BR>ReturnOfFiero@aol.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||10-25-2001||12:42 PM||||Email sent.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||10-25-2001||03:00 PM||||Oops.  Seems I could have avoided some confusion for the new Forum members by explaining what this is about.  This should answer it... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum7/HTML/000038.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum7/HTML/000038.html</A> <P><BR>We would like for anyone who's straddling the fence to consider joining CFOG-I for one year, and if you aren't satisfied then by all means cancel your membership and spread the word right here on PFF of your experience.  Make this offer to your local club too.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||10-26-2001||02:48 AM||||It is attitudes like Cheever3000's that will assure the success of CFOG-International. It is a pleasure to work with the people we have in the organization as Officers and Regional Directors. They have a tremendous knowledge of the Fiero as well as a drive and desire to unite the Fiero community.<P>Terry Owens, Chairman<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>CFOG-International</A>||||reg||1
